        <mxCell id="c73" value="Budget price as a share of list" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;fontSize=12;fontColor=#2C3E50;fontStyle=0;fontFamily=Helvetica;spacing=2;fillColor=none;strokeColor=none;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="448" y="364" width="220" height="20" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="c74" value="&lt;i&gt;The budget planned 88.1% of list in March and April, against at least 92.7% in the months with no promotion, so it planned a discount when the promotion ran; November is a little lower in every budget, the segment promotion&#x27;s month. The recorded end date, then, looks like a wrong entry, not discounts given outside the window. Promotions 1 and 7 show the same pattern. The axis starts at 86%.&lt;/i&gt;" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=12;fontColor=#5D6D7E;fontStyle=0;fontFamily=Helvetica;spacing=2;fillColor=none;strokeColor=none;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="0" y="392" width="860" height="53" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
